## Todo — Moonshots (Do Not Execute Yet)

> [!WARNING]
> The following 20 Moonshots must ONLY be worked on after the core compiler, standard library, and capability model are 100% stable. Many of these (like the Browser and Kernel) will require spinning up entirely new, isolated repositories. Do not let agents pick these up yet.

- [ ] **M1 — The Immune System (Continuous Mutation)**
  Where: `ooda/runtime/`
  What: Upgrade the Path-A static decoys into a fully live, continuously mutating metamorphic engine in RAM to prevent zero-day ROP chains.

- [ ] **M2 — Temporal Memory (Time-Travel Execution)**
  Where: `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_flight.c`
  What: Build a checkpoint/rollback hypervisor layer that logs capability traces and safely rewinds execution state upon panic.

- [ ] **M3 — Apoptosis (Programmed Cell Death)**
  Where: `std/src/ooda/concurrency/`
  What: Implement Erlang-style lightweight supervisor threads (`actor_spawn`). When a file exceeds 256 lines or a cell becomes corrupted, it triggers Apoptosis: gracefully deprecating itself and stripping export capabilities until a human/Swarm splits it.

- [ ] **M4 — Symbiosis (Mitochondrial Integration via Nexus)**
  Where: `openOODA/nexus/`
  What: Build the token-gated remote package manager. Quarantined third-party libraries that survive millions of execution cycles without violating mathematical contracts are automatically absorbed into the "Trusted Core" (Symbiosis).

- [ ] **M5 — Mathematical Resilience (SMT Solvers)**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Hook the `requires`/`ensures` syntax into Z3 (or similar SMT solver) to mathematically prove invariant safety at compile-time instead of runtime.

- [ ] **M6 — Hardware Quotas (CPU/Memory Sandboxing)**
  Where: `ooda/runtime/`
  What: Enforce strict OS-level memory `rlimit` bounds and `cgroup` cycle constraints mapped directly to `AllocCap` and `MAX_CYCLES`.

- [ ] **M7 — Cryptographic Call-Graph Integrity**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Sign all valid call edges at compile-time to instantly trap and terminate any ROP-chain anomalies at runtime.

- [ ] **M8 — Shadow-State Semantic Reversion**
  Where: `ooda/runtime/`
  What: Execute critical state changes (like global var mutations or DB writes) inside a ghost state, and automatically abort without committing if a panic occurs.

- [ ] **M9 — Telepathic AST (Intent-Driven Compilation)**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Embed an LLM daemon into the compiler that can synthesize full AST nodes from `// TODO` comments during the build step.

- [ ] **M10 — GPU/NPU Acceleration (PTX/ROCm)**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Native compiler backends to target graphics cards and neural processing units, gated by the `&GpuCap` capability.

- [ ] **M11 — Native Hot-Code Reloading**
  Where: `ooda/runtime/`
  What: Dynamically hot-swap compiled AST nodes inside a running binary process with zero downtime.

- [ ] **M12 — Data-Oriented Design (SoA Layouts)**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Automatically transform array-of-structs into struct-of-arrays memory layouts to maximize CPU cache-line hits and SIMD performance.

- [ ] **M13 — Token-Minimized Diagnostics (`--json-minimal`)**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Output ultra-compact JSON compiler errors specifically formatted to consume the minimum number of LLM context tokens.

- [ ] **M14 — Advanced Surgical AST Patching**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Upgrade the `ooda patch` tool to target exact AST Node-IDs instead of just replacing entire functions.

- [ ] **M15 — AI Symbol Reflection (`ooda context`)**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Allow an AI agent to run `ooda context path#symbol` to instantly dump the exact token-minimized type graph for a specific struct without reading the file.

- [ ] **M16 — Genetic Cross-Over (Global Hivemind Fuzzing)**
  Where: `openOODA/hivemind/`
  What: Build the P2P networking layer so idle compilers can autonomously clone the repo, splice random functions together (Genetic Cross-Over), and race them in the Thunderdome to continually mutate and evolve the `.oo` standard library.

- [ ] **M17 — openOODA Web Browser**
  Where: `openOODA/browser/` (New Repo Required)
  What: Build a native web engine in pure `.oo` where Javascript and WASM execution are strictly sandboxed by explicit capability tokens (e.g., physically unable to read local files).

- [ ] **M18 — openOODA Micro-Kernel**
  Where: `openOODA/kernel/` (New Repo Required)
  What: Build a bare-metal Operating System (similar to seL4) where raw hardware interrupts are mapped directly to granular capability tokens, removing the need for Linux `seccomp`.

- [ ] **M19 — Holographic Data Persistence**
  Where: `ooda/runtime/`
  What: Make databases obsolete by mapping variables in RAM directly to a persistent Merkle-tree on an NVMe SSD with zero serialization overhead.

- [ ] **M20 — Cross-Language Link-Time Optimization (LTO)**
  Where: `ooda/oodac/`
  What: Physically merge the `openOODA` AST with Rust's HIR to allow zero-overhead function inlining across the language boundary.

