## Lanes — swarm write ownership (folded from `LANE.oot` 2026-08-12)

**Purpose:** Orthogonal file ownership. No two write-agents own the same file.

### Rules

- **Write exclusivity:** each file path has at most one write-agent this turn.
- **Read-only lanes** may inspect any tree; they must not edit.
- **Power law:** ≤ **5** work items per agent per turn.
- If lanes would collide, stop and re-slice before Act.

### Current lanes (this turn)

| Agent | Lane | Trees |
|-------|------|-------|
| **agy** | std library | `std/` |
| **minimax** | sprint issues | follow their dirty files (do not steal paths they already hold) |
| **vibe** | audit (read-only) | monorepo (no writes) |
| **grok** | A process, B root hygiene, C runtime security residuals, D peer-verify, E QA/CI; **metamorphic path-A this turn** | `openOODA/` process docs, monorepo root hygiene, select `ooda/runtime` files, `qa/`, ooda CI; write: `rfcs/2026-08-11-metamorphic-path-a.oot`, `audit/meta_phalanx_rollup.oot` |

### How to use lanes

1. Pick work only inside your trees.
2. Before a write, confirm the path is not on another write-agent's dirty set.
3. Residual that crosses lanes: name it; do not silently edit peer trees.
4. Update this table when the coordinator reassigns lanes (same turn or next).

**Residual:** Lane map is turn-scoped. Stale rows after reassignment are hygiene debt — rewrite the table, do not accumulate ghost owners.

## Eighth sprint execution, 2026-08-11 (zero-trust audit fix swarm, rounds 1–3.5)

The seventh sprint recorded 50+ CRIT findings from a system-wide zero-trust audit. The user directed: "use a swarm and solve all of these yourself. grok is busy." I launched 5 rounds of 12-agent phalanxes (rounds 1, 2, 2.5, 3, 3.5) and folded the results here. **Net: every item the audit found in the tree is now either FIXED or DOCUMENTED AS RESIDUAL with the gap type named.**

### Per-round outcome

| Round | Scope | Result |
|---|---|---|
| **1** | DHE cleanup + DE1.1/1.2/1.3/1.4/1.5/1.6/1.7/1.8/1.9/1.10/1.11 + CIT 8.1 | 9 PASS, 1 PARTIAL (DHE: files were already gone), 1 blocked (HITL HOME — audit-side error: function `hitl_audit_open` doesn't exist; the actual code uses `oo_verify_human` with `oo_process_policy_getenv`). |
| **2** | DE2.1/2.2/2.3/2.4/2.5/2.6/2.7/2.8/2.9/2.10 + 3.x + 6.x + 7.x + 8.x | 10 PASS, 2 N/A (audit-side errors: HITL cap params referenced symbols that don't exist; SECRETSINK list was already covered in earlier rounds). |
| **2.5** | chs_rt_hash.c unused `j` + `__alias__` chain + HITL audit helpers + atfork + zc_emit_secret_oo brace-balance + LPAREN recursion + variadic args | 4 PASS (one agent discovered that round-4/5 rewrites had already replaced the audit-described functions; the audit's references were aspirational, not real). |
| **3** | dlopen signed `.so` (6.5) + `--runtime-cap-required` lint (6.12) + while_count.oo body build (8.4) + arc_smoke `\b` artifact (8.8) + strip CR from argv (8.6) + `${...}` lex branch (PV2.x) + `oo_list_quota_init_public` constructor (DE1.12) + doc tags + std crypto math stub | 8 PASS, 1 PASS-with-caveat (lint won't find symbols until emit-side is wired). |
| **3.5** | `oo_file_size` annotation + seccomp headers + `OO_FLIGHT_RECORDER_LOG` expression fix | 3 PASS, but verifier found 2 follow-on regressions (the `oo_file_size` fix landed in the wrong chain; the `OO_FLIGHT_RECORDER_LOG` was a statement `do {} while(0)` in a comma-expression context). Both fixed in this round. |

### What got fixed (file:line)

| Item | File | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| DE1.1 / PV1.1 | `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_host.c:25-46` + `chs_rt.h:188-191` | `oo_host_*` / `oo_chs_build` now take `&UnsafeFFICap` first arg, `oo_cap_require_ffi` at entry |
| DE1.2 / PV1.4 | `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_fs.c:103` | `oo_env_get` uses `oo_process_policy_getenv` instead of raw `getenv` |
| DE1.3 | (n/a — function doesn't exist) | `oo_process_policy_getenv("HOME")` already used by `hitl_audit_path()` (added in round 4) |
| DE1.4 | `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_sys.c` + `chs_rt_ffi.c` + `chs_rt_libfloor.c` + `chs_rt_time_rand.c` + `chs_rt_meta.c` | `pthread_once_t g_*_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT` for all 5 cap-init sites (round 1 + round 2.5) |
| DE1.5 | `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_sys.c:35-38` + `chs_rt_libfloor.c` + `chs_rt_time_rand.c` + `chs_rt_alloc.c` | Cap tokens widened from 32 → 64 bits (`0x1..000000000000LL` mask) |
| DE1.6 + DE1.7 | `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_alloc.c:82-87, 98-101` | `free_bytes` rejects `p > quota` (no clamp-to-0); `alloc_bytes` clamps to `LLONG_MAX` |
| DE1.8 | `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_sys.c:122-156` | `oo_sys_exec` filters env before `execvp`; only `OODA_*`/`OO_*` keys inherit, plus `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` |
| DE1.9 | `ooda/oodac/check_cap_util.oo:92-95` | `async_join_internal` + `python_embed_internal` added to `is_sealed_sys` |
