### What got documented as residual

- **2.12 / 5.1**: 8 std crypto "real" implementations (`ed25519_ops`, `dilithium_ops`, `groth16_ops`, `double_ratchet_ops`, `falcon_ops`, `kyber.oo`, `secp256k1_ops`, `plonk_ops`) are gated with `process_exit(1)`. Math not audited. The gate is load-bearing. Documented in `openOODA/openOODA/bootstrap/STDLIB_CRYPTO_MATH.oot` (new file, 79 lines).
- **chs_rt_v2.c**: audit-described but does not exist. Verified absent. Tagged `[STATUS: residual — chs_rt_v2.c was audit-described but does not exist; verified absent by Round 2.5 verifier]`.
- **String interpolation**: the lex branch is in place; the runtime c_emit lowering for STRING_TEMPLATE is staged. End-to-end `${secret}` refusal requires `token_scan_string.oo` to emit STRING_TEMPLATE tokens. Tagged `[STATUS: residual — string interpolation is a residual]`.
- **Function returns / aliases / field assigns / method calls**: most closed by Round 2 patches; closure-taint is a N/A until the language adds closure syntax. Tagged `[STATUS: residual — function returns / aliases / field assigns / method calls]`.
- **610 untracked std files**: triage only sampled 200. Remaining 410 are unverified. Not in scope of the zero-trust audit but worth flagging for the next phalanx.

